  "label": "The person is mapped as 'the fucking dishwasher'",
  "description": "The text 'the fucking dishwasher' is an analogical mapping that projects the visual entity 'person' onto the textual entity 'dishwasher'. The person is depicted interacting with the dishwasher in a frustrated manner, and the text explicitly labels the dishwasher as the source of frustration. This mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the visual scene (person struggling with dishwasher) and the text (focusing on the dishwasher as the 'culprit'), creating a humorous and exaggerated representation of domestic annoyance. The person's action and posture reinforce the mapping, as they are shown trying to fix or retrieve something from the appliance, which is the object of the text's frustration.",
